On the pale autumn sand sloping down to the water, Henri — an elderly man with short combed wavy white hair, a full white beard and white mustache, soft jawline, wearing a long blue coat, cream cable-knit wool sweater, grey wool trousers, black rubber boots, and a grey flat wool cap — sits on the beach, his hand pressing over his blue coat pocket as he looks down at his hands, his brows drawn together, eyes lowered, and mouth curved in a sad line. Near him, Léa — a toddler girl with loose chin-length straight dark brown hair and eyebrow-level bangs, brown eyes, wearing a long-sleeve orange knit sweater, blue denim leggings, and brown rubber rain boots — sits quietly on the sand, her eyes looking down at her lap with relaxed brows and a closed calm mouth. Next to her, Jules — a young school-age boy with combed short straight dark brown hair and bangs above his eyebrows, blue eyes, wearing a red hooded sweatshirt, grey cotton shorts-length jogger trousers, and white canvas sneakers — sits facing the sea with neutral features. Beside them, Élodie — an adult woman with loose mid-back wavy light brown hair parted in the center, brown eyes, wearing a long yellow wool cardigan coat, white long-sleeve cotton top, a long brown corduroy skirt, and tan suede ankle boots — turns slightly toward Léa with a calm, attentive expression. Marc — an adult man with combed short wavy dark brown hair parted at the side, stubble beard, brown eyes, wearing a green waxed jacket, grey crew-neck wool sweater, dark jeans, and brown leather lace-up boots — sits looking across at Henri with calm brows and mouth. Rust and ochre dune grass rises above them, fallen russet leaves scatter across the sand, and the distant pale coral reef line runs across the blue-green water under the clear afternoon sky. Wide shot across the autumn beach.

