At the foaming edge of the tide, Élodie — an adult woman with loose mid-back wavy light brown hair parted in the center, brown eyes, wearing a long yellow wool cardigan coat over a white long-sleeve cotton top — kneels on the damp shore, opening her hands to release the small fingers of Léa — a toddler girl with chin-length straight dark brown hair and eyebrow-level bangs, brown eyes, wearing a long-sleeve orange knit sweater — who stands upright before her. Élodie looks with calm brows, clear eyes, and a soft relaxed mouth directly into Léa's face, her fingers uncurling gently from the child's grasp. Léa looks up at Élodie with bright wide eyes, raised brows, and a beaming open smile, her boots resting at the wet foam line where tiny rounded stones and scraps of seaweed scatter across the sand. Close-up framing cropped above their waists, showing the foam line and sand beneath the warm autumn afternoon light.

---METADATA---
