In the wide underwater expanse before the reef wall, Gaspard — an olive-brown moray eel with cream-yellow spots, about chest-high in scale, large dark round eyes, and a low fin along his back — swells outward and fills the coral arch from side to side, his mouth stretched wide with brows pulled down in an angry scowl. Jules — a young school-age boy with short dark brown hair, blue eyes, wearing a short-sleeve blue swim shirt and a green mermaid tail — is thrown backward into the left midground, his arms flailing, fingers splayed with red scraped palms facing outward, his brows knitted and mouth open in an angry shout. Near the foreground sand on the right, Léa — a toddler girl with loose dark brown chin-length hair, brown eyes, wearing a long-sleeve green swim shirt and a smooth purple mermaid tail ending in a wide fin — floats motionless with both hands clutched tightly over her belly, her purple tail resting still in the water, eyes wide in fear, brows pulled upward, and mouth clamped tight. Broken coral fragments lie strewn across the sandy hollow beneath the arch under the deep blue water.

---METADATA---
