Under the glowing dusk sky where the sinking orange sun touches the sea horizon, Maëlle — an adult mermaid with long dark-teal hair, pale green eyes, wearing a pale sea-green top and a blue-green tail with a flared fin — lowers her brass hand bell to her side and swims steadily away along the crest of the distant coral wall toward the open ocean, only her upper back and trailing tail visible above the reef line. Far back on the darkening sand of the autumn beach in the foreground, Henri — an elderly man with combed white hair, full white beard, wearing a long blue coat, grey trousers, and a grey flat wool cap — stands alone at the water's edge, gazing out toward her departing silhouette, his hand sunk deep in his coat pocket, his stooped shoulders sagging, brows pulled down, and mouth set in a heavy sad curve. Ultra-wide vantage across the shore and the entire length of the coral wall under the twilight sea.

