In front of the rose and orange coral arch, Gaspard — an olive-brown moray eel with cream-yellow spots, chest-high in scale, soft rounded snout, and a closed mouth curved in a gentle, contented smile — slides smoothly backward into his sandy hole beneath the arch base, his rounded tail fin trailing into the shelter. With the archway now completely clear and open, Léa — a toddler girl with loose chin-length dark brown hair, brown eyes, wearing a long-sleeve green swim shirt and shimmering purple mermaid tail — floats happily at the arch's edge, her arms spreading wide, brows lifted, and mouth open in a bright joyful laugh as she watches Gaspard withdraw. Deep blue clear water surrounds the reef wall, where the sandy floor rests quietly beneath the open passage. Medium underwater shot centered on the open arch.

