At the open lip of the rose coral arch, Léa — a toddler girl with loose chin-length straight dark brown hair, bangs at her eyebrows, brown eyes, wearing a long-sleeve green swim shirt — brings both of her small hands up to cup around her mouth, leaning forward as she projects her voice outward through the empty coral arch toward the far end of the reef. Her brows are lifted with steady focus, her eyes wide and clear as she gazes straight into the archway, and her mouth is rounded open in a strong, steady call. Rough orange coral borders the frame above, with scattered coral crumbs across the sand below under the sunlit blue sea. Close-up framing cropped above her waist.

