From behind Léa — seen over her shoulder, cropped at the collar of her green swim shirt showing her loose chin-length dark brown hair — Léa floats at the open coral arch, looking outward along the reef wall that stretches away into the distance. Far down the reef at the last coral ridge, Maëlle — an adult mermaid with long wavy dark-teal hair and a blue-green tail with a flared fin — has turned mid-water and swims smoothly back toward the arch, her slender arms guiding her through the sunlit sea, her soft face turned toward Léa with gentle lifted brows and a warm happy smile. Pale sand and coral fragments line the foreground floor, while the coral wall recedes into deep blue water. Over-the-shoulder view looking out along the reef.

