At the pale coral rim of the rock beyond the coral wall, Maëlle — an adult mermaid with long wavy dark-teal hair falling to mid-back, pale green eyes, wearing a sleeveless pale sea-green cotton top — holds the brass hand bell forward by its loop handle with a warm, open smile. Reaching forward toward the bell, Jules — a young school-age boy with combed short dark brown hair, blue eyes, wearing a short-sleeve blue swim shirt — extends his hand, his fingers stretched eagerly to touch the polished brass rim, his brows raised high and mouth open in a delighted grin. Beside him, Léa — a toddler girl with loose chin-length dark brown hair, brown eyes, wearing a long-sleeve green swim shirt — floats with her hands clapping together in front of her chest, her eyes wide with joy, brows arched, and mouth beaming in a wide happy smile. Deep blue water surrounds the flat rock top. Close-up framing cropped above their waists.

