In the gentle dusk shallows of the autumn beach, Henri — an elderly man with combed white hair, full white beard, wearing a long blue coat, grey trousers, black rubber boots, and a grey flat cap — wades into the ankle-deep foam, extending both open hands forward with deep gratitude toward Maëlle — an adult mermaid with long wavy dark-teal hair, pale green eyes, wearing a pale sea-green top and a blue-green tail — who floats in the calm water with a warm smile, raising one hand in a wave as she begins to swim out on the ebb. Henri's face beams with high brows, joyful crinkled eyes, and a broad open smile. On the dry sand behind him, Léa — a toddler girl with loose chin-length dark brown hair, brown eyes, back on her legs in an orange sweater, blue denim leggings, and brown rubber boots — laughs with delight, wrapping her arms in a cheerful hug around herself as she looks at Henri with bright eyes and a wide grin. Beside her on the sand, Jules — in his red hoodie and grey jogger trousers — Marc — in his green waxed jacket and dark jeans — and Élodie — in her yellow cardigan coat and long brown skirt — all stand together smiling happily as they watch Maëlle depart toward the reef under the soft dusk sky. Wide shot of the autumn shoreline.

